## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-store consistency, idempotent writes, conflict handling, and disaster recovery across polyglot persistence in a real-time collaboration application.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotent multi-store writes across Redis, MongoDB, Cassandra, DynamoDB
- Cross-region conflict handling with eventual consistency
- Replay/restore path and tombstone semantics for recovery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: handle save edit across stores with client_write_id
async function saveEdit(doc, delta, clientWriteId) {
  // Redis: cache latest version atomically
  await redis.hSet(`doc:${doc.id}`, {
    content: doc.content,
    version: doc.version,
    clientWriteId
  });

  // MongoDB: upsert with revision tracking
  await db.documents.updateOne(
    { id: doc.id },
    { 
      $set: { 
        content: doc.content,
        version: doc.version,
        updatedAt: new Date(),
        clientWriteId
      }
    },
    { upsert: true }
  );

  // Cassandra: append immutable delta
  await cassandra.execute(
    'INSERT INTO document_edits (doc_id, rev, ts, user, delta, client_write_id) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)',
    [doc.id, doc.version, Date.now(), doc.userId, delta, clientWriteId]
  );

  // DynamoDB: update daily aggregates
  await dynamodb.update({
    TableName: 'daily_aggregates',
    Key: { doc_id: doc.id, date: new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0] },
    UpdateExpression: 'ADD edit_count :inc SET last_edit = :ts',
    ExpressionAttributeValues: { ':inc': 1, ':ts': Date.now() }
  });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-store writes with explicit TTLs and cache invalidation. It checks how writes propagate across Redis, MongoDB, Cassandra, and DynamoDB, plus how to keep a hot cache coherent.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-store write paths with idempotence
- TTL-based bucketing in Cassandra
- Cache invalidation and refresh strategies in Redis
- Read path with locality and fallback

## Code Example
```javascript
async function writeMessage(chatId, userId, text, ts){
  await redis.hset(`chat:presence:${userId}`, 'online', 1);
  const msgId = generateId();
  await mongo.messages.insertOne({chat_id: chatId, msg_id: msgId, sender_id: userId, ts, text});
  await cassandra.execute("INSERT INTO messages_by_chat (chat_id, bucket, ts, msg_id) VALUES (?, bucket(?), ?, ?)", [chatId, ts, ts, msgId]);
  await dynamo.archive({chat_id: chatId, msg_id: msgId, ts, text});
  await redis.publish(`chat:updates:${chatId}`, JSON.stringify({msg_id: msgId}));
}
```
